Subject: [PATCH] vtest: the VirGL route's frames into the app's buffers (VCMD_PD2_APP_PRESENT)

PD2 Launcher, our code (MIT, as virglrenderer). A new vtest command, VCMD_PD2_APP_PRESENT
(resource, flags; the answer is one word), and GET_PARAM VCMD_PARAM_PD2_APP_PRESENT, which says
whether the server can do it: on Android with vrend on EGL, when PD2_PRESENT_SOCKET names the app's
present socket and PD2_VIRGL_APP_PRESENT is not 0 (the debug switch back to the copy path). The
guest Mesa (userland/patches/mesa/0012) sends it at each front-buffer flush instead of reading the
frame back (TRANSFER_GET) for the X screen.

The server's child for that client becomes a client of the app's present server, with the
protocol of Mesa patch 0004 (HELLO, BUFFERS and the AHardwareBuffers, PRESENT with a fence,
RELEASE with a release fence; app/src/main/cpp/present_server.cpp). In an EGL context of its own
in vrend's share group (same config, OpenGL ES 3), it makes an EGLImage of each of the app's 4
buffers (EGL_ANDROID_get_native_client_buffer, EGL_ANDROID_image_native_buffer,
GL_OES_EGL_image), a texture and a framebuffer on it; for each frame it waits on the GPU for the
free buffer's release fence (EGL_KHR_wait_sync, else on the CPU), blits vrend's texture of the
resource into the buffer, takes an EGL_ANDROID_native_fence_sync fence and sends PRESENT (FIFO)
with it. A frame the app does not show now (the guest's WANTED flag clear) still sets up the
connection, so the app has a client. Answers: SHOWN; COPY (not this frame: not wanted, no free
buffer within 100 ms, a resource that is not 8-bit RGBA or BGRA UNORM, the app closed the
connection, after which frames of that size are not sent again); OFF (a missing extension or a
failed step: never again for this client, the connection closed so the app shows the X screen).
The new code is vtest/vtest_app_present.c; it is built only on Android with vrend and EGL, and
links libandroid.

---
